    "faq": {
      "type": "ces-faq-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "group_label": "",
            "question": "Does it hurt?",
            "answer": "<p>No. The micro-cones are far too small to reach the nerves that sense pain — most people feel only a light tingle or nothing at all.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "group_label": "",
            "question": "How is this different from an eye cream?",
            "answer": "<p>A cream sits on the surface, where most of it evaporates. CEBEAM's micro-cones dissolve below the barrier and deposit the actives into the layers where lines and dark circles form.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "group_label": "",
            "question": "How often should I use it?",
            "answer": "<p>During your reset, use one fresh two-patch treatment four nights per week. After completing the reset, maintain with two treatment nights per week. Each treatment is single use — a new sealed pouch every time.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "group_label": "",
            "question": "When will I see results?",
            "answer": "<p>Hydration and de-puffing are immediate. Dark circles and fine lines visibly improve by around week three — the end of the 21-Day Eye Reset — and firmness keeps rebuilding across the full 45-day course.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "group_label": "",
            "question": "Is it safe for sensitive skin?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The cones are made of hyaluronic acid and dissolve completely. If your skin is very reactive, start with two treatment nights a week and build up to four.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        }
      },
